List Items
List items are ordered, changeable, and allow duplicate values.
List items are indexed, the first item has index [0], the second item has index [1] etc.

List operations 
1.len 
2.Allow Duplicates
3.List datatypes 
4.Access list item 
5.Access sequence of Items
6.Change Item Value
7.Change a Range of Item Values
8.Append Items
9.Insert Items
10.extend()
11.Remove Specified Item
12.pop() method 
13.del method 
14.Clear the List
15.count 
16.sort 
17.reverse 
18.copy 
19.max 
20.min
21.dir 

#list
mylist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
print(mylist)

#len 
mylist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
print(len(mylist))

#Allow Duplicates
thislist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry", "apple", "cherry"]
print(thislist)
#List datatypes 
list1 = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
list2 = [1, 5, 7, 9, 3]
list3 = [True, False, False]
print(list1)
print(list2)
print(list3)

#Access list item 
thislist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
print(thislist[1])

#Access sequence of Items
thislist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry","grapes","chiku"]
print(thislist[2:5])

#Change Item Value
thislist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
thislist[1] = "blackcurrant"
print(thislist)

#Change a Range of Item Values
thislist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry", "orange", "kiwi", "mango"]
thislist[1:3] = ["blackcurrant", "watermelon"]
print(thislist)

#Append Items
thislist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
thislist.append("orange")
print(thislist)

#Insert Items
thislist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
thislist.insert(1, "orange")
print(thislist)

##extend()
thislist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
tropical = ["mango", "pineapple", "papaya"]
thislist.extend(tropical)
print(thislist)

#Remove Specified Item
thislist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
thislist.remove("banana")
print(thislist)

#pop() method 
thislist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
thislist.pop(1)
print(thislist)

#del method 
thislist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
del thislist[0]
print(thislist)

#Clear the List
thislist = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
thislist.clear()
print(thislist)

#count()
Counts occurrences.
lst = [1, 2, 2, 3, 2]
print(lst.count(2))

#sort()
Sorts the list.
lst = [3, 1, 4, 2]
lst.sort()
print(lst)

2 method 
lst = [3, 1, 4, 2]
lst.sort(reverse=True)
print(lst)

#reverse()
Reverses the list order.
lst = [1, 2, 3]
lst.reverse()
print(lst)

#copy()
Creates a shallow copy.
lst = [1, 2, 3]
new_lst = lst.copy()
print(new_lst)

#max() / min()
lst = [10, 5, 30]
print(max(lst))
print(min(lst))

